*> Implementation test of T6300 to T6302 (lane 002-lane-nethperf): the chunks of the Nether are made by the generation workers like those of the
*> standard overworld, so the game loop does not spend about 75 ms of every chunk (and, through the light of a sent chunk, the eight chunks round
*> it) on the generator: with a pool configured the in-tick queue leaves a Nether chunk to a worker, the chunk that arrives equals the in-process
*> reference byte for byte, a light neighbour that is not loaded is not generated where the light asks for it (WORLD-CHUNK-PEEK answers row 0), and
*> a chunk is sent only when its 3 x 3 neighbourhood is loaded (WORLD-LIGHT-READY, which also queues the missing ones). With no pool all of this is
*> as before. The fixture world has no netherrack in its block table, so the Nether chunk is the placeholder terrain (a pure function of the chunk).
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-NETHER-WORKER.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY COREAPI.
 COPY GENQUEUE.
 COPY GENSTAGE.
 COPY CELLS.
 01 WS-DIM                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 4.
 01 WS-STD                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 3.
 01 WS-CX                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CZ                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ROW                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TICKS               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-REF                 PIC X(304640).
 01 WS-REF-Y               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-A                   PIC X(304640) BASED.
 01 WS-WORKERS             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FLAG                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SLOT                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-RC                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SLEEP               PIC 9V99 VALUE 0.01.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-GEN-FIXTURE"

*>   the in-process reference of Nether chunk (2, 3)
     MOVE 2 TO WS-CX
     MOVE 3 TO WS-CZ
     MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-REF
     CALL "WORLDGEN-DIM-CHUNK" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ WS-REF WS-REF-Y

*>   with a pool the tick leaves the Nether chunk to a worker
     MOVE 1 TO WS-WORKERS
     CALL "GEN-WORKERS-CONFIG" USING WS-WORKERS
     CALL "GEN-QUEUE-WANT" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ
     CALL "GEN-QUEUE-TICK"
     CALL "WORLD-FIND" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ WS-ROW
     MOVE "test nether worker the dispatching tick leaves the Nether chunk to the worker" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-ROW TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "test nether worker the worker is busy with it" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE GW-BUSY(1) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     PERFORM WAIT-FOR-CHUNK
     MOVE "test nether worker the chunk arrives from the worker" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     IF WS-ROW > 0
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     ELSE
         MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     SET ADDRESS OF WS-A TO CK-ADDR(WS-ROW)
     MOVE "test nether worker the worker's Nether chunk equals the in-process reference byte for byte" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     IF WS-A = WS-REF
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     ELSE
         MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   a light neighbour that is not loaded is not generated by the light (row 0), and a read of the block does generate it as before
     MOVE 40 TO WS-CX
     MOVE 40 TO WS-CZ
     CALL "WORLD-CHUNK-PEEK" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ WS-ROW
     MOVE "test nether worker with a pool the light's peek at an unloaded Nether chunk answers row 0" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-ROW TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "WORLD-FIND" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ WS-ROW
     MOVE "test nether worker with a pool the peek loaded nothing" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-ROW TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   a chunk is sent when its 3 x 3 neighbourhood is loaded: the missing ones are queued, the chunk waits
     MOVE 2 TO WS-CX
     MOVE 3 TO WS-CZ
     CALL "WORLD-LIGHT-READY" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ WS-FLAG
     MOVE "test nether worker a loaded Nether chunk with no loaded neighbour is not ready to be sent" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-FLAG TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "test nether worker its eight neighbours were queued" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE GQ-COUNT TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 8 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-TICKS
     PERFORM UNTIL WS-FLAG = 1 OR WS-TICKS > 6000
         CALL "GEN-QUEUE-TICK"
         ADD 1 TO WS-TICKS
         CALL "WORLD-LIGHT-READY" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ WS-FLAG
         IF WS-FLAG = 0
             CALL "C$SLEEP" USING WS-SLEEP
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "test nether worker once the neighbours arrived from the workers the chunk is ready" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-FLAG TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   the idle worker stopped gracefully ends at the end of its input (its process leaves its coverage data behind)
     MOVE GW-SLOT(1) TO WS-SLOT
     CALL STATIC "cc_wk_stop" USING BY VALUE WS-SLOT BY VALUE 0 RETURNING WS-RC
     MOVE "test nether worker the idle worker stopped gracefully is reaped" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-RC TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO GW-SLOT(1)

*>   the standard overworld is not asked for its neighbours here (its light never generates them either)
     MOVE 5 TO WS-CX
     MOVE 5 TO WS-CZ
     CALL "WORLD-LIGHT-READY" USING WS-STD WS-CX WS-CZ WS-FLAG
     MOVE "test nether worker a standard chunk is always ready here" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-FLAG TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   with no pool everything is as before: the peek generates, the chunk is ready at once and nothing is queued
     CALL "GEN-QUEUE-RESET"
     MOVE 0 TO WS-WORKERS
     CALL "GEN-WORKERS-CONFIG" USING WS-WORKERS
     MOVE 60 TO WS-CX
     MOVE 60 TO WS-CZ
     CALL "WORLD-CHUNK-PEEK" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ WS-ROW
     MOVE "test nether worker with no pool the peek loads the Nether chunk as before" TO TL-CASE
     IF WS-ROW > 0
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     ELSE
         MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "WORLD-LIGHT-READY" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ WS-FLAG
     MOVE "test nether worker with no pool the chunk waits for its neighbours too" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-FLAG TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "test nether worker with no pool the missing neighbours were queued (the peek loaded the middle one, the 8 others are missing)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE GQ-COUNT TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 8 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   the in-tick queue makes them (two a tick), nothing is sent before then
     MOVE 0 TO WS-TICKS
     PERFORM UNTIL WS-FLAG = 1 OR WS-TICKS > 100
         CALL "GEN-QUEUE-TICK"
         ADD 1 TO WS-TICKS
         CALL "WORLD-LIGHT-READY" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ WS-FLAG
     END-PERFORM
*>   Two chunks a tick at most, but a chunk that takes the tick's wall time (GQ-MS-HUNDREDTHS) is the last of the tick (lane perfsteady): four ticks on a fast
*>   machine, up to one chunk a tick (eight) on a slow or loaded one. The case holds the count to that range.
     MOVE "test nether worker with no pool the in-tick queue made them within four to eight ticks" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF WS-TICKS >= 4 AND WS-TICKS <= 8
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   the view's far ring stays loaded one chunk further for the Nether (the light of the sent edge chunk), as the standard dimension's does not
     MOVE 2 TO CS-VIEW-DISTANCE
     MOVE CORE-SETTINGS TO CW-SETTINGS
     MOVE 1 TO PL-USED(2)
     MOVE PS-ALIVE TO PL-STATE(2)
     MOVE WS-DIM TO PL-DIM(2)
     MOVE 60 TO PL-CENTER-X(2)
     MOVE 60 TO PL-CENTER-Z(2)
     MOVE 1 TO WS-CX
     MOVE 1 TO WS-CZ
     CALL "CHUNKS-UNLOAD"
     MOVE 62 TO WS-CX
     MOVE 62 TO WS-CZ
     CALL "WORLD-CHUNK-LOAD" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ WS-ROW
     MOVE 63 TO WS-CX
     MOVE 61 TO WS-CZ
     CALL "WORLD-CHUNK-LOAD" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ WS-ROW
     CALL "CHUNKS-UNLOAD"
     MOVE 62 TO WS-CX
     MOVE 62 TO WS-CZ
     CALL "WORLD-FIND" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ WS-ROW
     MOVE "test nether worker a Nether chunk at the view distance stays loaded" TO TL-CASE
     IF WS-ROW > 0
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     ELSE
         MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 63 TO WS-CX
     MOVE 61 TO WS-CZ
     CALL "WORLD-FIND" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ WS-ROW
     MOVE "test nether worker a Nether chunk one beyond the view distance stays loaded too" TO TL-CASE
     IF WS-ROW > 0
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     ELSE
         MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 64 TO WS-CX
     MOVE 64 TO WS-CZ
     CALL "WORLD-CHUNK-LOAD" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ WS-ROW
     CALL "CHUNKS-UNLOAD"
     CALL "WORLD-FIND" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ WS-ROW
     MOVE "test nether worker a Nether chunk two beyond the view distance is unloaded" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-ROW TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "GEN-QUEUE-RESET"
     STOP RUN.

 WAIT-FOR-CHUNK.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-TICKS
     MOVE 0 TO WS-ROW
     PERFORM UNTIL WS-ROW > 0 OR WS-TICKS > 6000
         CALL "GEN-QUEUE-TICK"
         ADD 1 TO WS-TICKS
         CALL "WORLD-FIND" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ WS-ROW
         IF WS-ROW = 0
             CALL "C$SLEEP" USING WS-SLEEP
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM.
 END PROGRAM TEST-NETHER-WORKER.
 COPY CORETEST.
 COPY GENFIXTURE.
